from common import ROOT, load

def write_documents():
    r3 = load('results_R3.json')
    v = r3['measured_contrasts']
    (lo, hi) = v['conservative_difference_of_marginal95CI_pp']
    (ROOT / 'RESULTS.md').write_text(f"""# The drilling process may leave a measurable tissue state\n\nThe executable result carries thermal dose, regional damage and later biological measurements through a HANDOVER edge.\nTwo local primary studies are reference. They establish useful process-tissue relationships, but provide no validated\nprediction of human healing weeks or the ISQ of the implant, a measure from resonance rate analysis.\n\n| Question | Faktiskt svar | Resolution and reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| What does the sensor's binary temperature flag miss? | Six numerically described regions has approximately 0,2 – 1,1 mm damage despite associated probe peaks under 47 ° C . | Damage PER_SURFACE_REGION ; probe PER_POINT . [Purge et al.](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e26248), Table 2 and paragraphs p0105 / p0110 . |\n| Which observed protocol reaches the study's smallest reported damage width? | Ultrasound drilling, 2000 rpm, 60 mm/min , 4 mm drill, 20 kHz, 20 µm amplitude: approximately 0,2 mm in both cortical and cancellous bone . | PER_SURFACE_REGION, same study p0110. Medelkraft 4,05 ± 0,30 N. Cooling and width uncertainty missing. |\n| Is there a biological outcome after the drilling? | Dog bone fragments: 500 versus 1000 rpm has {v['viability_500minus1000_percentage_points']:.2f} percentage point higher viability today 3 -assay and {v['yield_day14_500_over1000']:.6f}× major cell growth at two weeks of culture. | POPULATION , n=4 reported group samples. [Zhou et al.](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-023-03611-w), Sec21 and Fig. 5 e/f. |\n| Can the temperature leave a spatial state ? | 28 existing K3 fields export the remaining tissue dose with coordinates and masks. Dry L10 model provides 0,15 mm lateral screening zone. | PER_POINT , 0,1 mm grid . Own existing simulation; empirical temperature magnitude failed in K3. |\n| What humane speeds, coolings, sequences and forces holds damage during a published safe boundary for a given bone ? | UNKNOWN. | No applicable validated boundary or parade process-damage-healing model is available in the substrate. |\n| How many weeks of healing delay or what ISQ course is predicted? | UNKNOWN. | The essential biological transfer act and a matched external reference are missing. |\n\n**0,2 mm is an observed comparator, no biological safety limit.** The oval study concerns ex vivo bone\nvid 22 °C. Its damage is defined as an area with more than 90 % empty osteocytoluenes. Three protocol has numerical\nwidths without SD . Lower temperature at a remote probe therefore gives no guarantee of the whole tissue state .\nProbe and cortical histology are not securely co-located; mechanical damage, starting viability and sample preparation may be\ndo not separate. The result rejects sensor as single total damage description, but rejects not a local thermal law\nat the actual drilling wall.\n\nThe dog test applies to harvested mandibulary fragments with 1 mm drill without flushing. T10 is a 10 second measurement window,\nno complete temperature history. The day of viability 3 is an assay time; the exact displacement from the operation is\nNot established here. Cell growth applies to two weeks of culture. ALP is measured after one week osteogenic induction and\nmineralisation after 21 day induction: these times must not be marked as post-operative healing days.\nThe biological measurements apply to bone fragments, not remaining bone around a implant.\n\nSD and n=4 provide under the assumption of independent normal distributed replicated margin t-ranges. The difference between\ntheir endpoints become {lo:.3f}–{hi:.3f} percentage points for 500 versus 1000 rpm. This is not a paired 95 % range.\nThe viability and ALP groups have different grades, but the viability ranges overlap in all three ranking turns.\nThe frozen gate for mid-range compliance fails ; a causal competence difference does not follow from this control .\n\nPublished risk support exists, but it does not close the numerical link. [Eriksson 1984 ](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6593442/)\nprovides a qualitative bone growth anchor at constant 44/47/50 ° C for one minute. [Kniha 2022 ](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-25581-9),\nTable 2/Results, describes necrosis and bone contact after seven days in rats. [Kniha 2023 ](https://doi.org/10.1186/s13005-023-00349-2),\nFig. 4 B, reports no statistically secured hot ISQ case after seven days; it does not mean shown absence\nof an effect. Miniature implants, various tissue support and missing paired time series prevent transfer to humane weeks.\n\n| Gate or failure | Reported outcome |\n|---|---|\n| R1, full temperature histories | 12/12 missing: exact dose validation UNKNOWN. |\n| R1, numerical injury protocols | 3 / 12 retained; 9 / 12 lacks numerical width. None of the six method pairs have both widths. |\n| R2, ovine observations to K3 | 6 / 6 rejected: other population and process. No data lending calibration. |\n| R2, robust width condition | 6/6 lacks the necessary width uncertainty. Two regions reaches nominal 0,2 mm comparison. |\n| R3, group relationships | 4/4 is retained. 4/4 individual/point relationships and 4/4 wall/ ISQ transfers are rejected. |\n| R3 , frozen viability contrast | 39,10 pp fails with 1,51 pp: the number applies to 50 against 1000 rpm but was marked 500 against 1000. Original retained. |\n| R4, new physiological measurements | 0. Own fixture only tests software. |\n\nEqually informed table outline and integration checks reproduce the result. No algorithm advantage is claimed.\nError injections rejects controls for temperature, dose/width/cell count units, missing calibration/region,\ndeleted tissue , wrong sample identity and fake security or ISQ - outputs . Valid technical controls holds .\nSource-outcome disclosure is available in the freezer files: R3 : s result was already read when the hypothesis was frozen . This is\nopen resolution and a new information interface, no blind prediction validation.\n\nRun `./run_all.sh` . It recreates raw extracts, tables, residual dose fields, figures and manifests without network.\n`bench_handover.py` can read a truly calibrated CSV . The integral is exactly for the linear temperature interpolant;\nThe sensor limits do not bind unsampled peaks and the dose remains a phenomenological liability for tissue measurement.\nMINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_CONTRACT.json describes the next same specimen design: temperature history, final histology\nand serial stability. Early destructive measurements needs separate cohorts and must not be given the same individual identity.\n\nThe existing goal graph is available in interfaces.jsonl. Rank, pack and dispatch gave STALE_INPUT ; no graphs were rebuilt.\nGRAPH_FEEDBACK.json is PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW and needs to be tied when the graph owner made the view up to date.\n""")
    (ROOT / 'README_DEMO.md').write_text("# From drilling to measurable tissue state\n\nThe idea is to leave an explicit state after drilling: local thermal dose, regional observed damage and\nseparate biological measurements. The demonstration shows what published data can determine and where the healing model\nstill missing support.\n\n```bash\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nRequires Python 3, numpy, scipy, matplotlib and the existing local sources in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json. No installation\nor network download is done. Maximum four threads. The result is available in RESULTS.md and machine readable in results.json.\n\n| Results | External reference |\n|---|---|\n| Three oval protocols have reported regional damage of about 0,2 – 1,1 mm . | Heliyon 2024, p0105/p0110; PER_SURFACE_REGION. |\n| UD 2000 rpm/60 mm/min has approximately 0,2 mm in both tissue types. | Same study, p0110. Observed comparison value, no safe boundary. |\n| 500 against 1000 rpm has 37,59 pp higher viability and 3,483 × cell growth at two weeks of culture. | Dog bone fragments, n=4 group samples; BMC 2023, Fig. 5e/f; POPULATION. |\n| 28 existing dose fields are given an interface for the remaining tissue. | K3 simulation; empirical temperature magnitude failed. |\n| Human safe drill parameters, healing weeks and ISQ. | UNKNOWN. |\n\n![Published measurements and biological handover](figures/X28_measured_handover.png)\n\nWhat does not holds : sensor temperature does not describe total regional damage; bone fragments is not implant wall;\nthree approximate damage widths cannot be a safe human boundary. Growing/induction days are not healing days.\nR3 : s frozen 39,10 pp contrast was mislabeled and fails ; the correct observation is 37,59 pp. Original retained.\nR3 : s source output had been read before the freeze, which is reported. No independent lab replication was performed.\nCustom fixture is only used for import, unit and identity checks.\n\nFor a real temperature measurement, fill BENCH_THERMAL_TEMPLATE.csv :\n\n```bash\npython3 bench_handover.py --thermal MIN_MATNING.csv --out MIN_HANDOVER.json\n```\n\nCSV requires the entire measuring window, calibration limit, pro placement, specimen /region/ tissue and remaining masks. All\npoint identities retained. The final histology of the same test can be linked to `join_injury`. No unknown healing stroke\nfilled in. Measurement requirements and identification limitations are available in MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_CONTRACT.json .\n\nLicenses: [Pourgiv et al., Heliyon 2024](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e26248) states CC BY-NC-ND 4.0\nfor the article. Only numerical facts are read and quoted; original characters and full text are not republished.\n[Zhou et al., BMC 2023 ](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-023-03611-w) indicates CC BY 4.0 ; extract and custom figures\nare processings of reported measurements . K3 is the project's own simulation. Its former ToothFairy2 background\nspecified CC BY - SA in the project data; no ToothFairy2 cases are read or exported in this round. No patient data are used.\n")
    (ROOT / 'HANDOFF.md').write_text('# X28 — four completed designs\n\nCapability : a command builds external damage measurements, the later biological measurement channels of bone fragments and 28 existing\ndose field as remaining tissue state. Calibrated laboratory histories can be imported with specific/region/time contracts.\nThe final goal — given bone type/process to damage limit, human healing weeks and ISQ — is still UNKNOWN.\n\nR1 : 12 temperature protocol is retained. 12 / 12 full dose stories are missing. Six numeric damage areas are missed by low\nprobe temperature. Sensor-only total injury fails ; the local thermal law at the drilling wall does not fold.\n3 / 12 protocols have numerical width; 0 / 6 method pairs have both numerical widths.\nR2 : 28 fields are exported with remaining masks. Dry L10 model: 0,15 mm lateral screening width of 0,1 mm grid .\nK3 : s empirical temperature gate is still FAIL . 6 / 6 ovina-to-K3-joins are rejected. UD 2000/60 has approximately 0.2 mm in\nboth tissue types. There is no robust width uncertainty or human safety limit.\nR3 : four group links from dog bone fragments. 37,59 pp viability contrast 500 -minus -1000 and 3,483221 × cell growth\nat two weeks of culture. Frozen 39,10 pp FAIL with 1,51 pp: error group label. All freeze files remain. Mean rank gate FAIL;\nall three reverse viability pairs have overlapping ranges. 4 / 4 point/individual and 4 / 4 wall -/ ISQ transfers are rejected.\nAssay/induction days are different from post-operative time; SOURCE_TIMING_CORRECTION.json retains the clarification.\nR4 : exact integral of linear T(t), dose range and same specific/region/tissue/population-join run. 47 ° C/60 s\nprovides 16 CEM43 - min ; 44 ° C / 60 s provides 2 . Own fixture verifies only software. Zero new physical specimen.\nTechnical controls and error injections holds. No independent physiological prediction validation has been performed.\n\nNext construction: same osteotomy site through calibrated heat history, final histology and serial stability,\nwith pre-registered damage/contact team and independent specimen for validation. Two thermopoints see a gradient but\ndoes not generally identify all heat source/cooling parameters. Early destructive assays require a separate cohort;\nNever connect them as the same individual specimen . Use MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_CONTRACT.json and bench_handover.py.\nRun no further scalar temperature ranking as replacement for these missing measurements .\n\nGraph: DENT-IF-TH-BONE-TEMP-FIELD found in notes/expansion/interfaces.jsonl. Working rank/packet/dispatch returned\nSTALE_INPUT. No rebuild or source/ generated graph mutation was performed. GRAPH_FEEDBACK.json is\nPENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. Missing coverage: native receiving node for residual tissue damage condition\nwith PER_POINT/PER_SURFACE_REGION support and a separate HANDOVER healing resolution. The ISQ consumer aggregates to\nimplant / PER_TOOTH only after contact geometry and calibrated time course. When the graph owner made the view fresh:\nDispatch X28 -heat-osseo with TASK_BRIEF.md and connect feedback to the current results.json -hash.\n')
